idium perfringens </italic>as a potential indicator for the Presence of Sewage Solids in Marine Sediments</article-title><source>Mar Pollut Bull</source><year>2001</year><volume>42</volume><fpage>31</fpage><lpage>35</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11382981</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/S0025-326X(00)00087-4</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B26"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Desmarais</surname><given-names>TJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Solo-Gabriele</surname><given-names>HM</given-names></name><name><surname>Palmer</surname><given-names>CJ</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Influence of Soil on Faecal Indicator Organisms in a Tidally Influenced Subtropical Environment</article-title><source>Appl Environ Microbiol</source><year>2002</year><volume>68</volume><fpage>1165</fpage><lpage>1172</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11872464</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1128/AEM.68.3.1165-1172.2002</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B27"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Solo-Gabriele</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Wolfert</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Desmarais</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Palmer</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Sources of E. coli to a SubTropical Coastal Environment</article-title><source>App Environ Microbiol</source><year>2000</year><volume>66</volume><fpage>230</fpage><lpage>237</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="B28"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Leeming</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Nichols</surname><given-names>PD</given-names></name><name><surname>Ashbolt</surname><given-names>NJ</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Distinguishing sources of fecal pollution in Australian inla